    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Burning Edict.</strong> When you cast Compelled Duel on a creature and it fails its saving throw, you ignore all of that creature’s damage Resistances when you deal damage to it, in addition to the spell’s normal effects.</p><p><strong>Saint’s Reprieve.</strong> When you must make a Death Saving Throw, you may expend a use of your Channel Divinity. If you do so, you regain Hit Points equal to your Paladin level + the roll of your Death Saving Throw. Until the start of your next turn, you can use a Bonus action to make an attack with Advantage on the roll.</p>"
